# netsurf: the QuickJS bridge's window services on the Vita
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# MacSurf's bridge implements location, history, scrolling, the viewport,
# document.title, alert/confirm and localStorage persistence only under
# __MACOS9__ (Carbon window list, StandardAlert, FSSpec files); elsewhere
# they were inert: location.href read "about:blank", nothing navigated.
# - quickjs/macos9.h: the services as a frontend API, switched on by
#   MACSURF_WINDOW_SERVICES; c = the script's own document.
# - macsurf_qjs.c: a MACSURF_WINDOW_SERVICES branch beside each __MACOS9__
#   one (the Mac code is untouched), and three deliberate differences:
#   * location reads THIS realm's document (with its #fragment, which
#     NetSurf keeps on the window), as document.cookie does (fixes879) --
#     not the front window, which during a load is still the old page;
#   * localStorage is keyed by ORIGIN: the Mac path hashes the whole page
#     URL into the filename, so no two pages of a site shared a store;
#     plain stdio, written to a temporary file and then renamed;
#   * location.replace() is native (no history entry) and
#     `window.location = url` navigates (PutForwards=href, as
#     document.location already did); both were missing on every platform.
#   Time the user spends reading an alert() is not charged to the script's
#   runaway deadline.
# - vita/js_platform.c: the Vita's services. Navigation and history steps
#   are queued on the scheduler, never run inside the script (MacSurf
#   navigated synchronously, under the running document); relative URLs
#   are joined to the document's (MacSurf passed them to nsurl_create,
#   which fails); a stale realm's request is dropped. history.go(n) walks
#   the top-level window's history, out of range does nothing.
#   alert/confirm: the system message dialog (sceMsgDialog); answered OK
#   at once during the autotest and in the simulator. localStorage lives
#   in ux0:data/VitaBrowser/LocalStorage/.
# - vita/window.c: scroll_to / scroll_pos. vita/main.c: page 18 JS-window
#   (testpages/pages/JS-window.html); a queued script navigation keeps a
#   page from counting as settled; dialogs auto-answer in the autotest.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 12.

